1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,925
This is Inbox Focus: your email, in order of importance.

2
00:00:04,925 --> 00:00:10,037
It shows first what needs you, summarises conversations and drafts the reply.

3
00:00:10,037 --> 00:00:12,412
Let's see how to install it and how to use it.

4
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:17,075
Start by downloading the installer from the releases page.

5
00:00:17,075 --> 00:00:20,911
There's the regular version and a demo version with fictional data,

6
00:00:20,911 --> 00:00:22,400
to try it without Outlook.

7
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:24,895
Run the installer.

8
00:00:24,895 --> 00:00:29,357
If Windows shows a warning, choose "More info" and "Run anyway".

9
00:00:29,357 --> 00:00:32,395
Installing over an older version keeps your data.

10
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,508
The first time, the app asks for your name,

11
00:00:36,508 --> 00:00:39,620
signature and how many days of email to analyse.

12
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:46,620
You also pick the AI: Claude, ChatGPT, Azure OpenAI, Gemini or a local model.

13
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:48,520
The Test button checks it works.

14
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:54,620
Each conversation gets a level, from P1, urgent, to P4.

15
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:59,078
The rules are clear: direct requests, deadlines, external customers,

16
00:00:59,078 --> 00:01:01,045
how long they've been waiting.

17
00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:04,312
And the app always explains why.

18
00:01:04,312 --> 00:01:07,300
If you disagree, change the level with one click.

19
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:12,117
Open an email and you get a summary of the whole conversation.

20
00:01:12,117 --> 00:01:16,180
Only the latest message is open, the earlier ones are one click away.

21
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:20,892
Tables and forwarded emails show up as in Outlook, and the AI reads them.

22
00:01:23,450 --> 00:01:26,900
The reply is already written, in the email's language.

23
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:31,567
Ask for changes in plain words, like "shorter" or "put it in a table",

24
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:33,700
and create the draft in Outlook.

25
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:36,262
The email moves to In progress right away.

26
00:01:36,262 --> 00:01:37,850
You always send it yourself.

27
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:41,986
Once you reply, the email doesn't disappear:

28
00:01:41,986 --> 00:01:44,792
it stays in Answered until you mark it done.

29
00:01:44,792 --> 00:01:48,880
The app shows when you replied and, if the other person goes quiet,

30
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:51,442
Prepare follow-up writes a short reminder.

31
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:55,800
The AI pulls the tasks out of the conversation.

32
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:59,078
Add your own, edit them, start them or tick them off,

33
00:01:59,078 --> 00:02:01,675
and the reply keeps up with your progress.

34
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:08,430
For the legwork, ask the AI for help: on one task or all of them at once.

35
00:02:08,430 --> 00:02:09,177
With Claude,

36
00:02:09,177 --> 00:02:13,780
Cowork handles the request and the result comes back to the app by itself.

37
00:02:15,110 --> 00:02:18,462
Notes like "discussed on the phone" stay with the email,

38
00:02:18,462 --> 00:02:23,010
and the AI takes them into account when it redoes the summary and the reply.

39
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:29,315
Invites have their own view, with date, location and calendar conflicts.

40
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:32,702
Accept or decline opens the response in Outlook.

41
00:02:34,010 --> 00:02:38,272
When you're done, press Done or Ignore, or archive to a folder.

42
00:02:38,272 --> 00:02:39,335
Made a mistake?

43
00:02:39,335 --> 00:02:42,997
Everything can be undone, and History keeps your changes.

44
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:49,210
Newsletters and automatic notifications go to Noise, away from what matters.

45
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:55,390
Inbox Focus never sends or deletes emails, and your data stays on your PC.

46
00:02:55,390 --> 00:02:58,602
Less time in the inbox, more time on what matters.
